SUMMARY:Freedom on the French Broad
DESCRIPTION:The Town of Marshall celebrates America’s 250th anniversary with a celebration in downtown Marshall \nHonoring our Heroes with a reading of our country’s founding documents on the historic courthouse steps in Downtown Marshall\, starting at 3:30 pm \n\n\nPledge of Allegiance \n\n\nA Reading of the Preamble to the Declaration of Independence \n\n\nAmerican Legion – Men and Women of Freedom presentation \n\n\nA sharing of North Carolina’s journey in our Country’s freedom and Madison County DAR history \n\n\nBlannahasset Island welcomes guests starting at 4 pm – don’t forget to bring your blankets and chairs as we enjoy a lineup of live music and fireworks. \n\n\n5:00 pm-6:00 pm – The Resonant Rouges \n\n\n6:30 pm-7:30 pm – Dulci \n\n\n8:00 pm-9:30 pm – The Back Pocket \n\n\n9:30 pm – Fireworks on the French Broad
URL:https://livemusicasheville.com/calendar/freedom-on-the-french-broad/
LOCATION:Downtown Marshall
CATEGORIES:Asheville Area,Live Music,Madison County
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://livemusicasheville.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/724484752_1317358653817292_4472929278944195283_n-e1782662240180.jpg
END:VEVENT
